DirectAudio — native Wine → Android AAudio mmdevapi driver
==========================================================

Original author / maintainer:
    The412Banner  <205237651+The412Banner@users.noreply.github.com>

Provenance:
    winedirectaudio.drv is an original driver. Wine has no AAudio backend
    upstream; this is a new native Wine mmdevapi driver written from scratch.
    Its structure and mmdevapi ring-buffer bookkeeping are modelled on Wine's
    own winecoreaudio.drv (the macOS CoreAudio backend), with the CoreAudio
    device layer replaced by Android AAudio — no PulseAudio daemon and no ALSA
    server in the path. Because it derives from and links Wine's LGPL-licensed
    mmdevapi internals, it is licensed LGPL-2.1 (see COPYING).

Contributions:
    Contributors retain copyright to their changes and agree to license them
    under LGPL-2.1-or-later. Add yourself below when you land a change.

    MaxsTechReview (Max, @maxjivi05)  —  2026-10-06
        The relay helper's field fixes (Droid-Deck/DroidDeck#338 "Fix Audio
        Crackling on Pulse & DirectAudio"): prime the ring before playing,
        fade out and re-prime on an underrun instead of zero-padding, one
        consumer per ring during a reopen, a 40 ms starting target kept
        across reopens, a device buffer of at least two bursts; and the
        PulseAudio sink's non-blocking half-burst servicing at audio
        priority. Carried into directaudio-relay.c and
        pulse/module-directaudio-sink.c in v1.4.0 / linux-v1.0.0.
